* British 900 SL preamp (V1a, V1b cathode follower, V2a, V2b, V3a, V3b cathode follower, tone stack, buffer and master),
* transcribed from the factory schematic of the 100 W single-channel head (drawing SLXa-61-02, page 2100-60-02 for the master
* and the effects loop). Read from a low-resolution scan: a few values (R21, the tone-stack pots) are the best reading of the drawing.
* The Direct and Record outputs (IC1a, IC2) are not in the audio path and are not modelled.
*
* Units: k M, m u n p. Node "0" is ground. See engine/include/sas/netlist.h for the format.

* Rail (node X): driven from the power amp at run time; 440 V is the standalone default.
V VRAIL x 100 440
* The guitar (or the pedal in front of the amp) behind a variable source resistance.
I VIN gin 1
R RSRC gin in 7k
* The guitar behind its source impedance. RSRC is the plain 7k source: the "Off" setting, and what a pedal in front of the amp
* looks like. A pickup replaces it with its own impedance as seen from the open-circuit voltage (the recording): the
* coil (winding resistance RPU + inductance) in parallel with its winding capacitance CPU and an eddy-current loss resistor
* RPL, then the cable capacitance (200 pF per 2 m, switched in steps of 200, 400 and 800 pF). The engine sets the values:
* single coil = coil 1 (2.5 H), humbucker and P-90 = coil 2 (5 H) with their own resistances; open = 1e12.
R RPU1 gin pkb1 1e12
.xfmr LPU1 L=2.5
  W pkb1 in 1 pu
.end
R RPU2 gin pkb2 1e12
.xfmr LPU2 L=5
  W pkb2 in 1 pu
.end
C CPU gin in 110p
R RPL gin in 1e12
R SWK1 in pkk1 1e12
C CCAB1 pkk1 0 200p
R SWK2 in pkk2 1e12
C CCAB2 pkk2 0 400p
R SWK4 in pkk4 1e12
C CCAB4 pkk4 0 800p

* Supply decoupling: R17 and C9 for V1 and V2a, R18 and C10 for V2b and V3 (33 uF each).
R R18 x b2 10k
C C10 b2 0 33u
R R17 b2 b1 10k
C C9 b1 0 33u

* Input, V1a (plate load R5, cathode R3 and C1) and the V1b cathode follower (plate on the rail).
R R1 in 0 1M
R R2 in g1 68k
T V1A g1 p1 k1 12AX7
R R5 b1 p1 220k
R R3 k1 0 2.7k
C C1 k1 0 1u
C C2 p1 k1 100p
T V1B p1 b1 k1b 12AX7
R R4 k1b 0 100k

* Gain control VR1 (1M, log) with its bright network: R21 and C13 in parallel before the pot, 1n from top to wiper.
C C3 k1b a1 22n
R R21 a1 a2 47k
C C13 a1 a2 470p
R VR1T a2 w1 1
R VR1B w1 0 1
C C22 a2 w1 1n

* V2a, then VR2 (1M, log) behind C14 and R24 / C15.
T V2A w1 p2a k2a 12AX7
R R7 b1 p2a 27k
R R6 k2a 0 2.7k
C C14 p2a a3 22n
R R24 a3 a4 470k
C C15 a3 a4 470p
R VR2T a4 w2 1
R VR2B w2 0 1
R R23 w2 0 1M

* V2b (plate load R9 with C4 across it), then C5 into the R11 / R12 divider.
T V2B w2 p2b k2b 12AX7
R R9 b2 p2b 100k
C C4 b2 p2b 1n
R R8 k2b 0 820
C C5 p2b a5 10n
R R11 a5 g3 220k
R R12 g3 0 220k

* V3a (plate load R13), directly coupled to the V3b cathode follower whose load R14 feeds the tone stack.
T V3A g3 p3 k3 12AX7
R R13 b2 p3 220k
R R10 k3 0 2.7k
T V3B p3 b2 k3b 12AX7
R R14 k3b 0 100k

* Tone stack (Marshall type): C18 and the 33k slope from the stack input; VR5 treble (220k), VR7 bass (220k, a rheostat), VR6 middle (22k).
C C18 k3b t 470p
R R28 k3b j 33k
C C20 j m 22n
C C19 j c19b 22n
R VR5T t wo 1
R VR5B wo m 1
R VR7 m nn 1
R VR6T nn c19b 1
R VR6B c19b 0 1

* R27 / R26 and the TL072 follower (IC1b), C7 into the master (VR1a and VR1b of the dual 10k pot, around the effects loop).
R R27 wo o1 680k
R R26 o1 0 68k
O IC1B o1 buf buf 0 NJM072
C C7 buf bm 22u
R VR1AT bm ms 1
R VR1AB ms mb 1
R R1M mb 0 3.3k
R VR1BT ms wb 1
R VR1BB wb mb2 1
R R2M mb2 0 3.3k
R R10M wb y 47k
R R11M y 0 220k
